Q2  Theta-approximants in Q(sqrt 17) and Q(sqrt -7): one embedding carries the full Hankel valuation
==============================================================================
  rho = 2^10/3^9, Theta mod 2^4000; alpha = u + v sqrt(d) with iota_1(alpha)/w = Theta mod 2^(P - v2(w))
   d |  n | v2(iota_1 N_n) | pred. L K_n + v2(T_n) + n v2(w) | v2(iota_2 N_n) | v2(Norm) | G_n^2 | Norm | arch. bound
   17 |  2 |            130 |                             130 |              2 |      132 | True  | !=0  | True
   17 |  3 |            500 |                             500 |              3 |      503 | True  | !=0  | True
   17 |  4 |           1260 |                            1260 |              4 |     1264 | True  | !=0  | True
   17 |  5 |           2550 |                            2550 |              5 |     2555 | True  | !=0  | True
      (approximant: log2 max(|u|,|v|,|w|) = 1332.4, v2(w) = 0, v2(u + v s - w Theta) >= 4000)
   -7 |  2 |            130 |                             130 |              4 |      134 | True  | !=0  | True
   -7 |  3 |            500 |                             500 |              6 |      506 | True  | !=0  | True
   -7 |  4 |           1260 |                            1260 |              8 |     1268 | True  | !=0  | True
   -7 |  5 |           2550 |                            2550 |             10 |     2560 | True  | !=0  | True
      (approximant: log2 max(|u|,|v|,|w|) = 1332.0, v2(w) = 0, v2(u + v s - w Theta) >= 4000)
  v2(iota_1 N_n) equals the prediction: the embedding that sees Theta carries the whole Hankel
  valuation, the other embedding contributes >= 0. This is the only 2-adic input of Theorem NQ.

==============================================================================
Q3  exact margin A_NQ(n) = L K_n + v2(T_n) + 2 log2 G_n - 2 log2(n! M0^K_n) at rho = 2^10/3^9
==============================================================================
  closed form of e_l(n) equals the defining sum for n < 120: True
  float log2 G_n agrees with the exact integer to 1.46e-11 bits (n < 26)
  leading coefficient of A_NQ(n)/n^3: +0.20621 bits (positive iff mu_bar < c_NQ)
  A_NQ(n):      n=10: -1245, n=50: -1.148e+04, n=100: 5.709e+04, n=200: 1.047e+06, n=400: 1.081e+07, n=800: 9.593e+07, n=1600: 8.064e+08, n=3200: 6.603e+09, n=6400: 5.344e+10
  A_NQ(n)/n^3:  -1.2454, -0.0919, 0.0571, 0.1309, 0.1688, 0.1874, 0.1969, 0.2015, 0.2039
  A_NQ(n) <= 0 exactly for n <= 72 among n <= 8000; positive for 73 <= n <= 8000
  quadratic equations of height <= 2^10: excluded at n = 75
  quadratic equations of height <= 2^100: excluded at n = 87
  quadratic equations of height <= 2^1000: excluded at n = 143
  quadratic equations of height <= 2^10000: excluded at n = 351
  (a root of A x^2 + B x + C with max|A|,|B|,|C| <= H has alpha = A Theta in O_K, w = |A| and
   |sigma(alpha)| <= 2H, so C_sigma <= (2n+1)H; exclusion needs A_NQ(n) > 2n log2((2n+1)H)).

