collatz_procgen_20260923_theta2_cube.py
rho = 2^10/3^9, mu_bar = 1.42647

==============================================================================
C1  parabola lemma: the X-orbit in the (a,b)-plane of G(rho^a, rho^b) = sum_k rho^(k^3 + b k^2 + a k)
==============================================================================
  functional equation G(rho^a, rho^b) = 1 + rho^(a+b+1) G(rho^(a+2b+3), rho^(b+3)) (mod 2^3000): True
  tails: sum_(k>=s) rho^(k^3) = rho^(s^3) G(rho^(3s^2), rho^(3s)), i.e. the point P(s) = (3s^2, 3s): True
  s < 60: nondegenerate parallelograms P(s1)+P(s2) = P(s3)+P(s4): 0;  collinear triples: 0
  (proof: s1+s2 = s3+s4 and s1^2+s2^2 = s3^2+s4^2 force {s1,s2} = {s3,s4}; equivalently
   (x1+y1)^2 + (x2+y2)^2 - (x1+y2)^2 - (x2+y1)^2 = 2(x1-x2)(y1-y2) != 0 for a sum pattern)
  v-direction: the points (0, n) lie on the line a = 0, which meets the parabola only at (0, 0) = X.

==============================================================================
C2  leading layers at the places 2 and xi: determinant valuation versus minimal matching
==============================================================================
  cost at place 2 (units L): c2(s) = (s+1)^3 - psi(s) (level m = 1);  at xi: cM(s) = psi(s) - s^3 (k = s)
  precision is set just above the minimal matching m0, so 'det valuation = m0' is decided exactly and
  'cancellation' means det valuation > m0
  psi   | place | #patterns | min matching unique | det valuation = min matching | cancellation seen
  raw   | 2     |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=-1  | 2     |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=-1  | xi    |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=0   | 2     |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=0   | xi    |        16 |                   0 |                            0 | 16
  c=1   | 2     |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=1   | xi    |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=2   | 2     |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=2   | xi    |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=3   | 2     |        16 |                   0 |                            0 | 16
  c=3   | xi    |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=4   | 2     |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  c=4   | xi    |        16 |                  16 |                           16 | 0
  => unique minimal matching <=> no cancellation; ties occur only where the leading cost is affine in s:
     c = 3 at 2 (c2 = 3s + 1) and c = 0 at xi (cM = 0); there the leading layer has rank one.

