==============================================================================
C5  v-direction: Z_n = G(1, rho^n) = sum_k rho^(k^3) (rho^(k^2))^n, Hankel determinants in n
==============================================================================
   n | v2 det(Z_(i+j)) | L n(n-1)^2(5n-4)/12
   1 |               0 | 0
   2 |              10 | 10
   3 |             110 | 110
   4 |             480 | 480
   5 |            1400 | 1400
   6 |            3250 | 3250
   7 |            6510 | 6510
   8 |           11760 | 11760
  Proof: Cauchy-Binet over subsets K = {k_1 < ... < k_n} of the nodes rho^(k^2); the term has valuation
  L[sum k^3 + 2 sum_(l<l') k_l^2], uniquely minimal at K = {0, ..., n-1}. The valuation is quartic,
  but the entries Z_n (n >= 1) are values of G off the X-orbit: they are not in Q + Q X, so under
  'X rational' the determinant is not an integer and gives no contradiction.

==============================================================================
C6  weighted and residue-class tails (Hermite-Pade companions)
==============================================================================
  sum_k k^j x^(k^3) = sum_(k odd) x^(k^3) mod 2 for j = 1..5: True  (over F_2 at most two companions survive)
  F_even(x) = sum_(k even) x^(k^3) = F(x^8); F_(0 mod 3)(x) = F(x^27): residue classes bring in the new
  numbers X(rho^8), X(rho^27) (the same problem at another rho, same mu_bar).
  two-sequence block-Hankel (rows: weight k^0 and weight k^1 tails, columns shifted):
   m | n = 2m | min-matching (bits) unique | v2 det
   1 |      2 | 80 (unique) | 80
   2 |      4 | 820 (unique) | 820
   3 |      6 | 3060 (unique) | 3060
   4 |      8 | 7640 (unique) | 7640
  dimension count (Siegel's lemma, type-I forms in r+1 companions with the common cube support):
    r = 0: needs mu_bar < 2.0000  -> within reach at mu_bar = 1.4265
    r = 1: needs mu_bar < 1.5000  -> within reach at mu_bar = 1.4265
    r = 2: needs mu_bar < 1.3333  -> OUT OF reach at mu_bar = 1.4265
    r = 3: needs mu_bar < 1.2500  -> OUT OF reach at mu_bar = 1.4265

